WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
01 / START WITH THE OPERATING PICTURE
Bookings, reporting history, and demand signals in the original dashboard.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
02 / ASK THE AGENT
Why is Harbor Cottage’s recommendation capped at $360?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
03 / GET A GROUNDED EXPLANATION
The reply explains the ceiling and move limit, and identifies its data sources.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
04 / KEEP THE CONVERSATION GOING
Ask about slower booking pace before deciding on a change.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
05 / CHECK BOOKING PACE
A fictional listing shows occupancy, booking pace, and proposed moves.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
06 / EXPLAIN THE MOVE AND CAP IT
Demand suggests $420. The $360 ceiling caps the proposal at +20%.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
07 / LET THE OPERATOR DECIDE
Review the proposed price and its reasoning before authorizing a change.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
08 / RECORD THE OUTCOME
The sample change log records the approved move and the operator.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
OR / LEAVE A PROPOSAL PENDING
No decision, no authorized price change. The proposal remains available.

